    {
      "id": "claim_94b05b12d7534f8b8a3c0efa4a90a4ef",
      "statement": "test_umlaut_transliteration and test_sharp_s_transliteration pin the seven-entry German transliteration map (ä→ae, ö→oe, ü→ue, ß→ss, Ä→Ae, Ö→Oe, Ü→Ue) and its ordering before NFKD/ASCII normalization: if normalization ran before the map, Müller would degrade to muller and these assertions would fail while accented-Latin tests kept passing.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://slugify.py#L24-L32",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ddbbd3904ec8e8f0bcc1128b0673935c97e2d2529429f476fbeea09481a3869f:"
