    {
      "id": "claim_4742b2894c7f4cc5892a9f2946003bb9",
      "statement": "test_unicode_normalization independently pins the NFKD/ASCII-ignore stage for accented Latin text — café→cafe, naïve→naive, résumé→resume — and keeps passing even if the transliteration map were reordered or emptied, because these inputs contain no umlauts; it is the group to update when the normalization step itself changes.",
