        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_4b930c751fe448f09d868719e6aee7bb",
      "statement": "Three test groups pin the hyphen-collapse stage from different angles: test_special_characters_removed shows punctuation between words becomes exactly one hyphen (Hello@World/Hello#World/Hello$World/Hello!World → hello-world, not helloworld and not doubled), test_numbers_preserved shows digits survive the [a-z0-9] class (Version 2.0 → version-2-0, Item 42 → item-42), and test_multiple_spaces_collapsed shows any run of spaces, hyphens, or interleaved separators collapses to a single hyphen (Hello - - World → hello-world).",
